WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.900
In true Marvel fashion, Captain Marvel's cast
is packed with fan-favorite actors.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.420
Alongside them is up-and-coming star Gemma
Chan, playing Starforce member Minn-Erva.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.540
Chan has risen through the ranks of British
television and film before appearing in a

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.120
few worldwide blockbusters.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.580
Here's where you've spotted her over the years.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.780
In 2009, Chan scored her first major credit
by appearing in a special episode of Doctor

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:27.740
Who alongside the popular Tenth Doctor, played
by David Tennant . "The Waters of Mars," which

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:32.830
won a Hugo Award, is set on the red planet
in 2059, where the Doctor encounters a human

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.320
colony which is endangered by his presence.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.860
Chan plays Mia Bennett, a geologist, who survives
the Doctor's unintentional meddling with the

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.020
structure of time.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.900
Chan didn't have a lot of screentime, but
the episode, which was one of Tennant's final

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:49.280
outings as the Doctor, was well-received,
setting her up for more roles in the future.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:56.280
A popular British sitcom that aired for four
series from 2006 to 2010, The IT Crowd revolved

00:00:56.290 --> 00:01:00.550
around three main characters, each of whom
brings different neuroses to their roles as

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.500
tech support for a major company.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:07.000
Chan appeared in two different episodes as
two different characters - after a brief initial

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.670
appearance in the 2010 episode "The Final
Countdown," she reappeared in "Reynholm vs.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:15.960
Reynholm" that same year, playing a Female
Sulu in a Star Trek parody.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:21.219
Chan followed up this appearance with a role
in the BBC series Sherlock, which stars Benedict

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.640
Cumberbatch and Martin Freeman as Holmes and
Watson, respectively.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:29.400
The hit show formats each classic Arthur Conan
Doyle story about the famous detective into

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.580
long installments that deliver a modern twist
on the tale.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.560
Chan appeared in the 2010 episode "The Blind
Banker" as Soo Lin Yao, a Chinese pottery

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.819
expert working at a museum who disappears
and turns out to have a dark past.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.580
"Some things aren't supposed to sit behind
glass.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.400
They're made to be touched, to be handled."

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.319
After smaller films and some guest spots,
Chan finally found a few recurring roles on

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.640
television shows, cementing herself as a star
on the rise.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:03.520
After her appearance on Sherlock in 2011,
Chan scored a series regular role in the fourth

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:08.500
series of Secret Diary of a Call Girl, which
was broadcast in both the U.K. and the U.S.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.660
Starring Billie Piper, best known for her
companion role alongside David Tennant on

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:17.269
Doctor Who, the show centered on Hannah, a
normal London girl by day who works as a call

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:18.780
girl at night to pay her bills.

00:02:19.129 --> 00:02:23.240
As her two lives continue to collide, she
meets new girls at the agency at which she

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.460
is employed, and that's where Chan comes in.

00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:29.760
During the fourth series of the show, she
played Charlotte, a haughty escort working

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.100
for the agency who is strident and always
gets what she wants.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:38.720
Chan followed up this huge role with a regular
spot on Bedlam, a British sci-fi drama, during

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.060
the show's second series.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:45.480
Starring Theo James, Bedlam tells the story
of Bedlam Heights, a run-down complex of apartments

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.320
home to a series of strange hauntings.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:52.180
Chan appeared as Keira, a childhood friend
of a character from the first series who serves

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:55.760
as a confidant for Ellie, the de facto lead
of the second series.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.000
"We've been drinking.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.040
It isn't safe to be in the pool."

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.700
"Paramedics and fun really don't mix."

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:07.340
Chan's first blockbuster breakout came in
Jack Ryan: Shadow Recruit in 2014.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:12.750
She appeared alongside Chris Pine as the namesake
CIA agent, Kevin Costner as the CIA official

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:17.239
who recruits him, director Kenneth Branagh
as a Russian tycoon, and Keira Knightley as

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.540
a medical student and Ryan's fianceé.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:24.180
Chan played Amy Chang, a fellow spy on Ryan's
team who proves herself to be an incredibly

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.180
competent ally.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.820
An extension of the Harry Potter universe,
Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them was

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:34.540
released to eager fans in 2016, moving the
magical world from the U.K. to the United

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.400
States during the 1920s.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:42.740
The movie introduces audiences to Newt Scamander
played by Oscar winner Eddie Redmayne, a "magizoologist".

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:47.040
Chan played Madam Ya Zhou, a member of the
International Confederation of Wizards.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:51.140
"You know which of your creatures was responsible,
Mr. Scamander?"

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:53.160
"No creature did this."

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.959
The film was a commercial smash, grossing
a total of $814 million, and was hailed by

00:03:58.959 --> 00:04:03.239
most critics as a promising start to a new
franchise within the already wildly popular

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.360
world of Harry Potter.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:09.540
Though Chan did not appear in the 2018 sequel,
her role in such a massive blockbuster set

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.560
her up for even more film success.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.700
Chan returned to a regular television role
in Humans, a British series for Channel 4

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:22.440
that aired between 2015 and 2018 and was also
broadcast on the American network AMC.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:27.080
Based on a Swedish show called Real Humans,
the series featured a world filled with hyper-realistic

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.460
robots called "synths."

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.080
Chan played a synth hired by a human family
to work as a nanny.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:36.069
Throughout her three seasons on the show,
Chan's standout performance attracted plenty

00:04:36.069 --> 00:04:37.080
of positive attention.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:43.080
Chan's biggest role yet came in 2018's Crazy
Rich Asians, the breakout hit adapted from

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.580
Kevin Kwan's bestselling novel of the same
name.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:51.440
As the first film since 1993's The Joy Luck
Club to feature an all-Asian cast and an Asian-American

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.880
lead, the film was both a critical and a commercial
success.

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.560
Chan played Astrid, a fabulously rich and
impeccably accomplished socialite who is so

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:02.800
successful and worldly that her husband has
grown resentful.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:07.580
Thanks to the first film's success, two sequels
are already in the works, and a mid-credits

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:12.280
scene indicated that one may focus heavily
on Astrid, as it shows her locking eyes with

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:14.740
a mysterious man at a luxurious party.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:20.340
2018's Mary Queen of Scots is a historical
drama based on the conflict between cousins

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.500
Mary and Elizabeth I to secure the throne
of England.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:28.640
Director Josie Rourke staged a soapy, feminist
spectacle with some groundbreaking casting

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.700
choices, including Chan's role.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:35.740
Chan played Bess of Hardwick, a close friend
of Elizabeth I who not only acted as the Virgin

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:40.440
Queen's confidante, but, alongside her husband,
helped keep Mary captive for 15 years.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:44.860
Even though Chan's casting was technically
historically inaccurate, Rourke insisted on

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:49.660
color-blind casting, giving Chan an opportunity
to make a big impression before her debut

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.560
in the MCU.

